/**
 * @page tool_remote Going remote
 *
 * The transport is local by default; going remote is one argument at each end.
 *
 * On the **device side**, listen where the client can reach you:
 * `usbip_transport(NULL, 3240)` (or `"0.0.0.0"`) binds every interface, while
 * `"127.0.0.1"` binds only the loopback, which a remote client can never reach.
 * Open TCP 3240 in the firewall.
 *
 * @code{.c}
 * usb_transport *transport = usbip_transport(NULL, 3240);
 * usbip_device_plug(dev, transport);          // serve on the network
 * @endcode
 *
 * On the **host side**, point the context at the serving machine:
 *
 * @code{.c}
 * usb_transport *transport = usbip_transport("10.0.0.5", 3240);
 * usbip_host_set_transport(ctx, transport);
 * @endcode
 *
 * An OS importer attaches the same way from anywhere:
 * `usbip attach -r <server-ip> -b 1-1` (@ref clients).
 *
 * Speed declarations, isochronous pacing and the latency cost of a network round
 * trip per transfer are covered in @ref cl_hw.
 */
